What changed
------------

The fork is the Colophon render worker. It is not the upstream hosted
compile service.

- Each job runs in a new rootless Podman container (`--network=none`,
  read-only root, 512 MiB tmpfs, non-root user, 1 CPU, 256 pids, 60 s wall
  clock, 20 MiB output cap). The address-space ceiling is `RLIMIT_AS`
  (default 2048 MiB, `COLOPHON_RLIMIT_AS_BYTES`). Podman 4.4 and newer
  receive `--ulimit as=`. Podman 4.3 rejects that flag, so the worker
  injects the rlimit with a precreate hook that crun applies. A wall
  clock at or after 60 s is `failTimeout`, including Podman 4.3 exit 255.
  `GET /v1/host-load` is the token-gated load report (`loadavg`,
  `memAvailableMiB`, `activeJobs`, `queued`, `reportedAt`). There is no
  `/load` path.
  `--memory=2048m` and `--memory-swap=2048m` are set only when the cgroup
  memory controller is available. Without it (for example
  `cgroup_disable=memory`) both flags are omitted and the process logs a
  warning. Soft and hard are both `2147483648` by default. A missing `cpu` controller refuses
  startup. Preflight requires `cpu` and `pids`; memory is optional.
  `RLIMIT_AS` limits virtual address space per process, not resident set
  size and not the whole container (worst case 256 × 2 GiB; one job at a
  time, few TeX processes, and the MemAvailable shed bound it). An
  allocation failure is `failCapHit`, the same outcome as an early
  SIGKILL. The 2048 MiB default is enough for the measured XeLaTeX and
  LuaLaTeX jobs. The container is removed afterwards. The result is returned in
  the HTTP response and is not kept.
- LaTeX shell-escape is off (`-no-shell-escape`, and `shell_escape = f` in
  the image texmf). The host compiler path raises rather than running TeX
  on the worker host.
- The listener binds only to one configured address (`COLOPHON_BIND_ADDRESS`)
  inside the required `COLOPHON_BIND_ALLOWED_CIDR`. It refuses to start if
  either is unset, if the address is unspecified (0.0.0.0 or ::), a hostname,
  loopback, link-local, multicast, RFC1918, outside the CIDR, or `is_global`.
  A unique-local address is allowed only when it is inside the CIDR. Common
  examples of that CIDR are `100.64.0.0/10` and `fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48`.
- `GET /version` returns the package version and the git commit or tag baked
  at image build time (`COLOPHON_GIT_COMMIT`), plus a link to that revision
  in this repository. The image also sets the OCI revision label.
- Every request needs the shared worker token (Bearer). Concurrency is one
  job per process. A second job is refused at once with Retry-After. There
  is no queue.
- New jobs are refused when the 1-minute load average is above 3.0, when
  MemAvailable is below 4096 MiB, or when the load sample is stale or
  unreadable. An unreadable kill-switch file is treated as engaged.
- Spawn failures, Pandoc failures, diagram failures, and LaTeX failures
  fail closed. A wall-clock kill is `failTimeout`, which is not a render
  error. Output over 20 MiB is `failCapHit`.
- `POST /builds/sync` still accepts a single inline TeX or Markdown resource,
  but URL, git, tar, and cache resources are rejected, and the only compiler
  is XeLaTeX.
- The image bakes a trimmed TeX Live (XeLaTeX, xeCJK, Noto CJK TC, TikZ,
  CircuiTikZ) plus Pandoc, the pandoc-ext/diagram Lua filter (TikZ engine
  only), and a vendored PIDcircuitTikZ. Chromium, Node, mermaid-cli, and
  d2 are not installed. There is no runtime package fetch and no Tectonic.
  `tlmgr` is removed from the image. No Asymptote binary is installed.
  Jobs that ask for shell-escape, `\write18`, minted, the TikZ `external`
  library, Asymptote, gnuplot, epstopdf, the `svg` package,
  `\feynmandiagram`, an un-starred `\diagram`, or a fenced Mermaid or D2
  block are refused before compilation. The patterns match TeX directives
  and fences, not prose. `\vertex` and `\diagram*` stay allowed.
  `packages-once.tex` is an install check only.
- TeX Live packages, by tlmgr name and not via `scheme-full`: `circuitikz`,
  `siunitx`, `pgfplots`, `chemfig`, `mhchem`, `tikz-3dplot`, `tikz-feynman`,
  `tikz-cd`, `forest`, `tikz-timing`, `bytefield`, `pgfgantt`,
  `tikz-dimline`, `tikzscale`, and `pgf` (TikZ libraries `shapes`,
  `arrows.meta`, `positioning`, `calc`, `automata`, and `mindmap`). These
  are the files shipped by the Debian `texlive-pictures` and
  `texlive-science` collections already in the image.
- `colophon-v1-preamble.tex` is the one engine preamble. The TeX wrapper,
  the Pandoc template, and TikZ diagram blocks input it. It loads
  `circuitikz`, `siunitx`, `pgfplots`, `chemfig`, `mhchem`, `tikz-3dplot`,
  `tikz-feynman`, `tikz-cd`, `forest`, `tikz-timing`, `bytefield`,
  `pgfgantt`, `tikz-dimline`, `tikzscale`, `colophon-floorplan`, the TikZ
  libraries `shapes`, `arrows.meta`, `positioning`, `calc`, `automata`,
  and `mindmap`, and `\usetikzlibrary{circuits.pid.ISO14617}`. A fence
  option cannot replace that list. The PID library replaces TikZ's `at`
  and `pos` keys; the preamble puts those two keys back so chemfig and
  ordinary nodes keep working. PID symbols still load.
- `colophon-floorplan.sty` is installed in the local texmf tree. It defines
  the TikZ styles `floorplan wall`, `floorplan door`, `floorplan window`,
  `floorplan room label`, `floorplan scale bar`, `floorplan north arrow`,
  and `floorplan dimension`. Room area is computed from the corner numbers
  (`w*h*plan-scale^2/10^6`, or the shoelace helper
  `\floorplanPolygonArea`). The dimension label uses coordinate anchors, so
  `scale=` and tikzscale do not change it. Labels use `siunitx`. The style
  file is pure TeX.
- A failed render returns a result class (`ok`, `failTimeout`,
  `failCapHit`, `renderError`, or `refused`), wall time, `memory.peak` and
  `pids.peak` from the job cgroup, and on a render error the first TeX
  or TikZ diagram diagnostic (message, file, line, fence index). When the
  sandbox reports it, `memory.mode` is `cgroup` or `rlimit`. The success
  body stays the artifact. Meters for a success are the `X-Colophon-Job`
  header. `X-Colophon-Result` stays `ok`. Without the memory controller,
  `memory.peak` is null.
- Sold-candidate kinds are P&ID, circuits, plots (pgfplots, including a
  small 3D sample), chemistry, Gantt, and floor plans, plus the document
  shell. Mermaid and D2 are not kinds. A kind is not claimed sold here.
  `tikz-cd`, `forest`,
  `automata`, `mindmap`, `tikz-3dplot`, `tikz-feynman`, `tikz-timing`, and
  `bytefield` stay in the preamble and are smoke-compiled only. The
  tikz-feynman refusal of `\feynmandiagram` and un-starred `\diagram` stays.
- Fenced diagrams in HTML and DOCX are images from the diagram filter.
  Inline `siunitx` and `mhchem` notation is typeset in PDF only. HTML and
  DOCX keep that command text in the artifact and add `warnings` with code
  `notationPdfOnly` on `X-Colophon-Job`. The result class stays `ok`.
- `GET /version` includes `packageSet` and `packageSetHash`. The set is the
  sorted TeX package names in `colophon/package_set.txt`, including
  `colophon-floorplan`. The image build writes that list to `PACKAGE_SET`
  after checking each `kpsewhich` name. The hash is the sha256 of the names
  joined by newlines, with no trailing newline. The request reads the baked
  file and does not run a shell.

Third-party pieces added with this fork
----------------------------------------

- pandoc-ext/diagram, commit 5aaf35e6f775ddf501045fe28b03642ee73db2f4,
  MIT, with local edits (see vendor/diagram/README.md). SHA-256 of the
  vendored diagram.lua:
  f37001cabcda9061264552523eb36ba22ecc328f7026dae4b5bc14599b98da1b.
  Debian `librsvg2-bin` supplies `rsvg-convert`, which Pandoc uses to place
  SVG diagrams in a PDF.
- PIDcircuitTikZ by Jelle Spijker, MIT. There is no CTAN package of this
  name (CTAN search, 2026-09-26). It is not CircuiTikZ. CircuiTikZ is the
  CTAN package `circuitikz`. TikZ is delivered by CTAN package `pgf`.
  xeCJK is CTAN package `xecjk`. Debian bookworm ships it in
  `texlive-lang-cjk` as `xeCJK.sty` (kpathsea is case-sensitive). Noto CJK
  TC is installed from Debian `fonts-noto-cjk`, not from CTAN.

Busy and load-shed responses use `Retry-After: 10`. Request bodies above
16 MiB are refused.
